# Put a Staff of the Abyss in a character's hands, identify it, and open the
# item description screen, which is where the game renders the staff's page.
# Read by tools/check_staff_abyss_spell_list.sh, finding PA-08-F7 of
# bd inc-tek.8.8.
#
# WHY THE DESCRIPTION SCREEN AND NOT THE FILE. This finding changes prose and
# nothing else, so no behaviour moves and no behavioural check is possible.
# The honest oracle is therefore the page as the PLAYER reads it, not the page
# as lib/m_items.irh stores it: grep over the source would prove only that a
# file changed. Item::Describe prints the entity's Desc through DESC(eID)
# (src/Help.cpp:3405-3408), and Inventory Mode's 'x' puts that on screen
# (src/Managers.cpp:751-754), so this script drives the game to the same
# screen a player would reach and lets the check read the rendered words.
#
# WHY THE PACK IS IDENTIFIED. Item::Describe prints the entity's page only
# when the item isKnown(KN_MAGIC) (src/Help.cpp:3405). Wizard mode's
# "Identify Whole Pack" calls MakeKnown(0xFF) on everything the character
# carries (src/Debug.cpp:717-720).
#
# WHY A BARBARIAN IS ENOUGH. The staff is inert in the hands of a good
# character or of anyone below five caster levels -- that is its EV_MAGIC_HIT
# gate. The gate gives or withholds the SPELLS; it has nothing to do with the
# description screen, which reads the entity's Desc string off the resource.
# tools/keys/chargen.keys makes an orc barbarian, and that is all this reading
# needs.
#
#   w y                    enter wizard mode and open its menu.
#   Item Acquisition       RIGHT*3 walks the glyph row to Staves: ItemGlyphs
#   RIGHT*3                (src/Tables.cpp:320-323) puts -AI_STAFF three
#                          steps along.
#   @until "Staff of       the candidate list has no menu letters, so the
#     the Abyss" DOWN      cursor is walked. Three rows show and the MIDDLE
#   DOWN*3                 one is selected, so the @until stops one row EARLY
#                          -- on the pass where the Abyss first appears, as
#                          the row below Winter. The Abyss is the last staff
#                          entity in lib/m_items.irh and the list is in file
#                          order, so there is no row after it to walk to and
#                          the extra DOWNs saturate harmlessly. The check does
#                          not trust any of that: it reads the staff's name
#                          back off the description box's own title line.
#   ENTER 2 ENTER          take it, and answer "Enter Item Level:" with 2,
#                          which is the plus the page states (src/Debug.cpp:
#                          604-620).
#   b SPACE s              the pickup drops the staff into the in-air slot and
#                          opens Inventory Mode. 'b' is the Weapon Hand -- the
#                          slot lettering skips 'd', which is the Drop key --
#                          SPACE swaps the staff into it (src/Managers.cpp:873)
#                          and 's' stows the starting knife that swap pushed
#                          into the air, because the manager will not close
#                          while anything is held there
#                          (src/Managers.cpp:835-848).
#   ESC i b x              leave the manager, reopen it once the pack is
#                          identified, put the cursor back on the Weapon Hand
#                          and press 'x', which describes what is in it.
#   DOWN*6 five times      this staff's page is long -- the entity even carries
#                          EF_DLONG -- and the box shows about forty rows at a
#                          time, scrolling one row per DOWN
#                          (src/TextTerm.cpp:537-540). Six dumps at six-row
#                          steps put the whole page in front of the check and
#                          guarantee that at least one of them holds the spell
#                          sentence entire, which is what it has to count.

@include chargen.keys

w
y
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*3
@until "Staff of the Abyss" DOWN
DOWN*3
ENTER
2
ENTER
b
SPACE
s
@dump:staff-wielded
ESC
w
@choose "Identify Whole Pack"
i
b
x
@dump:desc-1
DOWN*6
@dump:desc-2
DOWN*6
@dump:desc-3
DOWN*6
@dump:desc-4
DOWN*6
@dump:desc-5
DOWN*6
@dump:desc-6
ESC
ESC
